VERDICT: the SMAD arm validates (rho 0.494, BH 6.15e-09) -- a firmer footing than either
ligand transcript. BUT the dissociation control ALSO validates (rho 0.619, BH 2.83e-09), and predicts the target program
BETTER. So the association is NOT separable from a generic activation
program at donor level, and it may NOT be described as TGF-beta-specific.
The defensible claim stays at the AGGREGATE niche-signalling level.
(The target program itself contains ACTA2, TAGLN, SERPINE1, IL6, CXCL2,
ICAM1, VCAM1 -- an activation program -- so this confound is expected,
not surprising, and no amount of donor-level modelling will remove it.)
